CDDA 0.I: avoid per-quad heap allocations during mapbuffer saves.

Every save_quad() handles exactly four submaps, but the current implementation
builds two std::vectors and calls reserve(4) on each for every saved quad.
Use fixed-size std::array storage and hoist the invariant overmap-to-submap
conversion out of the four-element loop. Preserve offsets/order, serialization,
uniform-submap handling, and deletion behavior.

